sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, one Swamp run, Ansible phases for idempotent Node state (rule 22), swamp refused at admission. docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#native-role-relocation.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:role:relocate
  %% kind: node.role_relocate
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>gets the role
  participant S as Source Node<br/>gives up the role
  CLI->>GW: node:role:relocate<br/>NODE ROLE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:relocate NODE ROLE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--from=NODE] [--force] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the target Node and the role: `gateway`, `websocket` or `metrics`
  %%> - `--from` names the source; without it, the current holder is the source
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  opt role is swamp
    GW--xCLI: 422 swamp role held<br/>node.role_relocate_swamp_held
    %%> Why:
    %%> - serve on the Swamp Node runs every Swamp run, so a run cannot move it; nothing is recorded
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, move the role
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node
  %%> - the target is active, has recorded SSH management and holds no conflicting role (`node.role_conflict`)
  %%> - the role is relocatable, assigned and `active` (or `failed` or `provisioning` in a retry), and `--from` owns the move
  %%> - consent: `--force`, or the CLI prompt, asked only after these checks pass
  %%> - one add, converge, remove or relocate Operation per target Node (`operation.target_busy`)
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - for `websocket`, the Reverb `APP_KEY` copied only when the target lacks one; for `metrics`, the role credentials the target lacks, without overwriting any; for `gateway`, the access grants to the `vpn` and `metrics` Nodes
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the assignment moves to the target and stays `active`, so the role is never out of service
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-relocate
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt role is metrics
    SW->>N: Apply the Metrics role<br/>child operation-metrics-enable
  end
  opt role is websocket
    SW->>N: Build the Reverb release<br/>Ansible phase: release
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - clones and checks out the Reverb ref as the Node's user, installs its packages, writes its private `.env` and unit, and switches the release link
    %%> - the target needs Git, PHP and Composer
    SW->>N: Start Reverb<br/>Ansible phase: service
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - enables and restarts the unit, then checks that Reverb answers on its port
  end
  opt role is gateway
    SW->>N: Add the DNS route<br/>Ansible phase: dns-route
    %%> Best effort:
    %%> - a failed route on the target reports `follow_up` and does not stop the move
  end
  opt role needs a certificate
    SW->>N: Publish the certificate<br/>child role-certificate-publish
  end
  opt role is websocket or gateway
    SW->>N: Open the role ports<br/>Ansible phase: firewall
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - opens the role's ports on the target and closes the retired ones
  end
  SW->>N: Publish the Caddy sites<br/>child operation-route-caddy
  %%> Order:
  %%> - the target serves before anything leaves the source; the source's sites are not published again
  SW->>N: Publish the role DNS<br/>child route-dns-publish
  opt private DNS moved
    SW->>SW: Let DNS answers expire<br/>child route-dns-grace
    %%> Why:
    %%> - clients that still hold the old answer keep working until it expires
  end
  SW->>S: Remove from the source<br/>child node-role-remove
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the role's runtime and publications from the source and forgets its settings there; for `gateway` it does not stop Caddy or PHP-FPM, so clients on the old address keep working
  %%> - for `metrics` it keeps the fleet exporters and the `metrics.orbit` name and certificate, which the moved role uses
  SW->>N: Check the role<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the one end check: Reverb answers, the ports, sites and DNS are in place on the target
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the role active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role is `active` on the target, and the task succeeds
    %%> Next:
    %%> - relocation does not reconcile Metrics; `follow_up` names the `node:role:add METRICS-NODE metrics --converge` command when a Metrics role exists and `websocket` or `gateway` moved
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Keep the role active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role already belongs to the target and stays `active`; a demoted `gateway` role would lock the Gateway out of its own access checks
    %%> - the task fails with the step's own code, and the failed step stays on the Operation: `converge:STEP`, or `remove:Remove from the source` when the source removal failed
    %%> Who serves:
    %%> - after a target step failure the source still serves, because DNS moves after the target steps; after a source removal failure the target serves
    %%> On the Nodes:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause and run the same command with `--from`; a cancelled or interrupted run leaves the claim `provisioning`, and the retry takes it over
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
